# Team Kit workflow for ZK-Coprocessor

This repo uses Cursor Team Kit for local validation and shipping. Prefer these skills over ad-hoc checklists.

## When to invoke

- After adding or changing TypeScript/Rust/circuit code: run `check-compiler-errors` before claiming the change works.
- Before opening or updating a PR: use `review-and-ship` or `new-branch-and-pr`.
- When CI fails on a PR: use `fix-ci` or `loop-on-ci` (with `gh pr checks` as source of truth).
- When asked to prove a fix or performance claim: use `verify-this` with baseline/treatment artifacts under `/tmp/verify-this/<claim-slug>/`.
- Before a harsh maintainability pass on prover/circuit glue: use `thermo-nuclear-code-quality-review`.
- After AI-heavy edits: run `deslop` before review.

## Project constraints

- Keep imports at file top (Team Kit `no-inline-imports`).
- Exhaustive `switch` on unions/enums with a `never` default (Team Kit `typescript-exhaustive-switch`).
- Do not invent compile/test success — re-run the repo’s real check commands.
- Order: `research-first-deep-tech` → implement → `test-and-validate-e2e` → `commit-push-after-success` → next step. Use `tooling-autonomy` when a skill/MCP/CLI is missing.
- This workspace may start sparse; if there is no compile target yet, say so explicitly instead of skipping silently.
